sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client (or Employee)
    participant Biz as Business service<br/>(e.g. CheckoutService)
    participant Pub as NotificationOutboxPublisher<br/>(DomainEventPublisher)
    participant Reg as NotificationEventMapperRegistry
    participant Map as OrderPlacedEventMapper<br/>(subdomain-owned)
    participant DB as App DB<br/>(aggregate + notification_outbox)
    participant Relay as OutboxRelay<br/>(scheduled)
    participant Kafka as Kafka<br/>(notification-events)
    participant Listener as NotificationEventListener
    participant Dispatch as NotificationDispatchService
    participant Tmpl as TemplateResolver
    participant SenderF as NotificationSenderFactory
    participant Sender as EmailNotificationSender<br/>(or SMS / Push)
    participant NDB as Notification DB

    rect rgb(235,242,250)
    note over Client,DB: Phase 1 — business transaction (producer side)
    Client->>Biz: place order / register / change status
    activate Biz
    Biz->>DB: INSERT/UPDATE aggregate (e.g. Order)
    Biz->>Pub: publish(OrderPlacedEvent)
    activate Pub
    Pub->>Reg: resolve(OrderPlacedEvent.class)
    Reg-->>Pub: OrderPlacedEventMapper
    Pub->>Map: map(orderPlacedEvent)
    Map-->>Pub: NotificationEvent (canonical)
    Pub->>DB: INSERT notification_outbox row (status=PENDING)
    deactivate Pub
    Biz-->>Client: 200 OK
    deactivate Biz
    note right of DB: Same DB transaction commits both rows atomically —<br/>aggregate change and outbox row succeed or fail together.
    end

    rect rgb(255,244,230)
    note over Relay,Kafka: Phase 2 — relay (async, decoupled from the request)
    loop every outbox-poll-interval
        Relay->>DB: findPending(batchSize)
        DB-->>Relay: List<NotificationOutbox> (PENDING rows)
        loop for each pending row
            Relay->>Kafka: send(NotificationEvent)
            alt broker acknowledged
                Kafka-->>Relay: ack
                Relay->>DB: markPublished(id)
            else publish failed
                Relay->>DB: markFailed(id, error)
                note right of Relay: row stays PENDING/FAILED,<br/>retried on next poll
            end
        end
    end
    end

    rect rgb(232,245,233)
    note over Kafka,NDB: Phase 3 — Notification Service (consumer side)
    Kafka->>Listener: deliver NotificationEvent
    activate Listener
    Listener->>Dispatch: dispatch(event)
    activate Dispatch
    Dispatch->>Tmpl: resolve(event.eventType, event.locale)
    Tmpl-->>Dispatch: NotificationTemplate
    Dispatch->>Dispatch: render subject/body from event.templateData
    Dispatch->>SenderF: getSender(recipient's channel)
    SenderF-->>Dispatch: NotificationSender
    Dispatch->>NDB: save Notification (status=PENDING)
    Dispatch->>Sender: send(notification)
    activate Sender
    alt delivery succeeded
        Sender-->>Dispatch: success
        Dispatch->>NDB: update status=SENT, sentAt=now
    else delivery failed
        Sender-->>Dispatch: error
        Dispatch->>NDB: update status=FAILED
    end
    deactivate Sender
    deactivate Dispatch
    Listener-->>Kafka: commit offset
    deactivate Listener
    end

    rect rgb(250,230,230)
    note over Listener,Kafka: Phase 4 — retry / dead-letter (failure handling)
    loop periodic retry
        Dispatch->>NDB: find FAILED notifications
        Dispatch->>Sender: send(notification) (retry)
    end
    note over Listener,Kafka: If the listener itself repeatedly fails to<br/>process a message, it is routed to<br/>notification-events-dlq for manual inspection.
    end
